          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "ProseTrial.lean — the sealed source"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "{\n \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\",\n \"name\": \"ProseTrial.lean\",\n \"url\": \"https://uuidna.com/lean/ProseTrial.lean\",\n \"inLanguage\": \"lean4\",\n \"variableMeasured\": {\n  \"@type\": \"PropertyValue\",\n  \"name\": \"theorems\",\n  \"value\": 6,\n  \"unitText\": \"theorem\"\n }\n}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-orbits_number_six",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The ledger walks exactly six distinct orbits. Six, and the count is the whole vocabulary — a seventh would be a word nothing proves."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "orbits.length = 6"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem orbits_number_six : orbits.length = 6 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-order_measures_orbit",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "THE ORDER IS THE LENGTH. A walk's order — the period any motion derived from it must have — is exactly how many digits its orbit reaches, taken by the kernel rather than asserted: [10, 8, 3, 1, 6, 4]."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "orbits.map (fun o => o.length) = [10,8,3,1,6,4]"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem order_measures_orbit : orbits.map (fun o => o.length) = [10,8,3,1,6,4] := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-forged_order_refused",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A FORGED ORDER IS REFUSED, and the refusal is on this line. Move one order by one and the derived list no longer equals it — so a period a person chose can never pass as a period the walk actually reaches."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(orbits.map (fun o => o.length) = [10,8,3,1,6,4]) ∧ (orbits.map (fun o => o.length) ≠ [10,8,3,1,6,5])"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem forged_order_refused : (orbits.map (fun o => o.length) = [10,8,3,1,6,4]) ∧ (orbits.map (fun o => o.length) ≠ [10,8,3,1,6,5]) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-orbits_reflect_onto_themselves",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Every orbit is closed under the reflection dz(x) = 10 − x: the mirror of each member is already a member, so reflecting a finished walk adds no digit and the vocabulary cannot grow by looking at itself."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "orbits.all (fun o => o.all (fun d => o.contains (dz d)))"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem orbits_reflect_onto_themselves : orbits.all (fun o => o.all (fun d => o.contains (dz d))) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-orbits_are_distinct",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "No two of the six are the same walk — the vocabulary has six words and not five wearing six names. Pairwise distinct, decided rather than assumed."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(orbits.map (fun o => o.length)).eraseDups.length = 6"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem orbits_are_distinct : (orbits.map (fun o => o.length)).eraseDups.length = 6 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-every_orbit_holds_zero",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Zero is in every orbit: dz fixes it, so no walk can leave it behind. The one digit every handle in the ledger reaches, whatever it folds from."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "orbits.all (fun o => o.contains 0)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem every_orbit_holds_zero : orbits.all (fun o => o.contains 0) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
